																		Re: &#039;The London Brick Incident&#039; First draft
															</div>
				<div class="info">
					<span class="printuser avatarhover"><a href="http://www.wikidot.com/user:info/plaguepjp" onclick="WIKIDOT.page.listeners.userInfo(5813664); return false;"  ><img class="small" src="http://www.wikidot.com/avatar.php?userid=5813664&amp;amp;size=small&amp;amp;timestamp=1609878561" alt="PlaguePJP" style="background-image:url(http://www.wikidot.com/userkarma.php?u=5813664)"/></a><a href="http://www.wikidot.com/user:info/plaguepjp" onclick="WIKIDOT.page.listeners.userInfo(5813664); return false;" >PlaguePJP</a></span> <span class="odate time_1600714445 format_%25e%20%25b%20%25Y%2C%20%25H%3A%25M%7Cagohover">21 Sep 2020 18:54</span>
														</div>
			</div>
			<div class="content" id="post-content-4779706">
									

<p>Sorry this took so long.</p>
<div class="collapsible-block">
<div class="collapsible-block-folded"><a class="collapsible-block-link" href="javascript:;">+&nbsp;Text&nbsp;critique</a></div>
<div class="collapsible-block-unfolded" style="display:none">
<div class="collapsible-block-unfolded-link"><a class="collapsible-block-link" href="javascript:;">-&nbsp;Text&nbsp;critique</a></div>
<div class="collapsible-block-content">
<blockquote>
<p>SCP-XXXX is to be remained quarantined at its origin point at the Site ██</p>
</blockquote>
<p>It's kind of counter-intuitive to redact the cite of containment. If I'm reading this file how will I know where to go?</p>
<blockquote>
<p>Requested was permitted by senior researcher Dr ██████ and an MTF Beta-7 squad of was sent into SCP-XXXX to retrieve a sample.</p>
</blockquote>
<p>Unneeded following the previous sentence.</p>
<blockquote>
<p>Upon attempting to retrieve a sample, the SCP-XXXX-2 entity reanimated, and with it several others who began to breach containment, but were all terminated before they could do so, though outpost 4 and four watchtowers were destroyed in the process, and left only 7 survivors of the attacked areas. The following is a statement given by the Captain Myers of the Beta-7 squad 5-A sent into SCP-XXXX-1.</p>
</blockquote>
<p>If you have an interview log following this paragraph describing the same thing it's kinda unnecessary.</p>
</div>
</div>
</div>
<div class="collapsible-block">
<div class="collapsible-block-folded"><a class="collapsible-block-link" href="javascript:;">+&nbsp;Overall&nbsp;critique</a></div>
<div class="collapsible-block-unfolded" style="display:none">
<div class="collapsible-block-unfolded-link"><a class="collapsible-block-link" href="javascript:;">-&nbsp;Overall&nbsp;critique</a></div>
<div class="collapsible-block-content">
<p>First and foremost, I'd like for you to remove the redactions you have, other than the one in the autopsy log. Mainly, they're an eyesore to read through and I'd also have you come up with the creative information that is being hidden. I also pointed out the counterintuitiveness of redacting the Site location of SCP-XXXX, along with that redacting the names of doctors is a slightly tired practice of the wiki.</p>
<p>This is slightly enjoyable but fails in the meat of the anomaly. There is a lot of telling the reader, here's what the -2 instance was doing, here's why there's the honey-like substance around vital organs. The O5 log at the end is probably the main offender here, especially with that lack of most of the information being told. In the description, you don't describe SCP-XXXX-1 other than mentioning a factory. The O5 log is honestly the real issue I see. There's no actual show of the anomaly's power other than the testimony of the MTF agent. You should definitely delve into the real horror of these spore creatures. There's a lot of room for body horror that is unrealized as well. There's a lot of mentioning of the potential threat of SCP-XXXX-2, the point I want to hit here and I'll keep hitting is that it's never shown. Show it to me in action.</p>
<blockquote>
<p>Though now I would like some feedback on the autopsy report to see if it's necessary and add anything to the article.</p>
</blockquote>
<p>I think the autopsy report was the most well-written part of this file. There's a good sense of build-up, pretty solid dialogue, and body horror. With that we gained the information that the spore creatures are somewhat intelligent. I'd say keep it. If anything, rework the final interview.</p>
<p>A smaller point, there's a bit of a stigma against having a bunch of collapsible bunched together. I personally don't normally use collapsibles for this reason, but if you'd like to present the article in this way I recommend looking at <a href="/scp-5982">SCP-5982</a> or other <span class="printuser avatarhover"><a href="http://www.wikidot.com/user:info/rounderhouse" onclick="WIKIDOT.page.listeners.userInfo(4187885); return false;"><img class="small" src="http://www.wikidot.com/avatar.php?userid=4187885&amp;amp;size=small&amp;amp;timestamp=1601334669" alt="Rounderhouse" style="background-image:url(http://www.wikidot.com/userkarma.php?u=4187885)" /></a><a href="http://www.wikidot.com/user:info/rounderhouse" onclick="WIKIDOT.page.listeners.userInfo(4187885); return false;">Rounderhouse</a></span> articles to see how he presents collapsibles in a pleasing way.</p>
</div>
</div>
</div>
<p>Good luck!</p>

							</div>

								
